\subsubsection*{1.3 Generator Comprehensions}

A generator comprehension \texttt{(expr for x in xs)} is a concise
generator expression. Like a generator function, it is lazy and
one-shot: the same comprehension object can be iterated only once.

The loop variable is captured by reference (late binding). If the
comprehension references an outer variable that changes after the
comprehension is built, the change is visible when the comprehension is
consumed.

Nested comprehensions \texttt{(y for x in xs for y in x)} flatten one
level of structure, applying the inner \texttt{for} at each outer
iteration.
